\newlabel{subsec:method_overview}{{{2.1}}{2}{Architectural Overview and Method Pipeline}{subsection.2.1}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Computational architecture and recombination inference pipeline of \texttt  {RhizAeon}\xspace  .} The four-stage processing workflow transforms raw multiple sequence alignments into exact, model-calibrated characterizations of reticulate evolution in linear time without discrete tree reconstruction or combinatorial triplet enumeration. \textbf  {Stage\nobreakspace  {}1 (Metric Manifold Embedding):} Sequential Farthest-Point Minimax Sampling extracts $N \ll M$ diverse reference landmarks from $M$ genomes in $\mathcal  {O}(M \cdot L)$ operations. Classical multidimensional scaling (MDS) embeds landmark distance matrices into a fixed $d$-dimensional Euclidean manifold ($\mathbb  {R}^d$, $d \in [2, 4]$) where orthogonal axes represent fundamental Buneman phylogenetic bipartitions. Gower out-of-sample projection continuously tracks any isolate as a spatial trajectory $\mathbf  {z}_i(u) \in \mathbb  {R}^d$ across all positions $u \in [1, L]$ without sliding window re-embedding. \textbf  {Stage\nobreakspace  {}2 (Directed Attention \& Root Sink Decoupling):} Tree-RoPE rotary phase embeddings encode Buneman metric distances into complex attention rotations, coupled with a continuous-time Markov substitution prior that discounts invariant vertical sites and elevates rare shared synapomorphies. An ancestral Root Sink token (node zero) anchored at the metric origin absorbs lineage-specific mutational bursts (heterotachy, APOBEC editing), preventing spurious donor affinity. The resulting position-specific attention tensor $A_u(i \to j)$ integrates into a cumulative differential flux curve $Y(u) = C_{\text  {Donor}}(u) - C_{\text  {Home}}(u)$. \textbf  {Stage\nobreakspace  {}3 (Three-Tier Hierarchical Statistical Inference):} Inference addresses the three evolutionary regimes of recombination. First, Tier\nobreakspace  {}1 resolves macroscopic single crossovers via centered Brownian bridges $B(u)$ with closed-form Kolmogorov extreme-value boundaries. Second, Tier\nobreakspace  {}2 isolates short gene conversions (50--300 nt) via a multi-scale bank of zero-mean bipolar dyadic wavelets $h_\tau $ convolved continuously across all $u \in [1, L]$ in $\mathcal  {O}(L)$ time, paired with running drawdown $\text  {DD}(u)$ to capture momentum collapse at exit. Third, Tier\nobreakspace  {}3 resolves multi-parental mosaics via multidimensional restoring force vectors $\mathbf  {f}(u) \in \mathbb  {R}^d$, singular value decomposition (SVD) mode peeling, and parameter-free halting at the Marchenko-Pastur bulk spectral noise edge ($s_{\text  {bulk}}$). \textbf  {Stage\nobreakspace  {}4 (Profile Polishing \& Output Inventory):} Candidate breakpoints are refined using profile maximum likelihood polishing under the fitted nucleotide substitution model, identifying the uninformative gap and biological uncertainty bounds. Continuous spatial mode polarity ratios ($p_{\text  {mono}}$) objectively classify reticulation topologies, outputting an authenticated event roster and interactive WebAssembly dashboards.\relax }}{3}{figure.caption.1}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:method_overview}{{1}{3}{\textbf {Computational architecture and recombination inference pipeline of \RhizAeon .} The four-stage processing workflow transforms raw multiple sequence alignments into exact, model-calibrated characterizations of reticulate evolution in linear time without discrete tree reconstruction or combinatorial triplet enumeration. \textbf {Stage~1 (Metric Manifold Embedding):} Sequential Farthest-Point Minimax Sampling extracts $N \ll M$ diverse reference landmarks from $M$ genomes in $\mathcal {O}(M \cdot L)$ operations. Classical multidimensional scaling (MDS) embeds landmark distance matrices into a fixed $d$-dimensional Euclidean manifold ($\mathbb {R}^d$, $d \in [2, 4]$) where orthogonal axes represent fundamental Buneman phylogenetic bipartitions. Gower out-of-sample projection continuously tracks any isolate as a spatial trajectory $\mathbf {z}_i(u) \in \mathbb {R}^d$ across all positions $u \in [1, L]$ without sliding window re-embedding. \textbf {Stage~2 (Directed Attention \& Root Sink Decoupling):} Tree-RoPE rotary phase embeddings encode Buneman metric distances into complex attention rotations, coupled with a continuous-time Markov substitution prior that discounts invariant vertical sites and elevates rare shared synapomorphies. An ancestral Root Sink token (node zero) anchored at the metric origin absorbs lineage-specific mutational bursts (heterotachy, APOBEC editing), preventing spurious donor affinity. The resulting position-specific attention tensor $A_u(i \to j)$ integrates into a cumulative differential flux curve $Y(u) = C_{\text {Donor}}(u) - C_{\text {Home}}(u)$. \textbf {Stage~3 (Three-Tier Hierarchical Statistical Inference):} Inference addresses the three evolutionary regimes of recombination. First, Tier~1 resolves macroscopic single crossovers via centered Brownian bridges $B(u)$ with closed-form Kolmogorov extreme-value boundaries. Second, Tier~2 isolates short gene conversions (50--300 nt) via a multi-scale bank of zero-mean bipolar dyadic wavelets $h_\tau $ convolved continuously across all $u \in [1, L]$ in $\mathcal {O}(L)$ time, paired with running drawdown $\text {DD}(u)$ to capture momentum collapse at exit. Third, Tier~3 resolves multi-parental mosaics via multidimensional restoring force vectors $\mathbf {f}(u) \in \mathbb {R}^d$, singular value decomposition (SVD) mode peeling, and parameter-free halting at the Marchenko-Pastur bulk spectral noise edge ($s_{\text {bulk}}$). \textbf {Stage~4 (Profile Polishing \& Output Inventory):} Candidate breakpoints are refined using profile maximum likelihood polishing under the fitted nucleotide substitution model, identifying the uninformative gap and biological uncertainty bounds. Continuous spatial mode polarity ratios ($p_{\text {mono}}$) objectively classify reticulation topologies, outputting an authenticated event roster and interactive WebAssembly dashboards.\relax }{figure.caption.1}{}}
