\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Continuous sequence metric manifolds resolve competing retroviral chimeras in linear time without triplet enumeration.} \textbf  {(A)} Canonical Sequence Metric Space: Classical multidimensional scaling (MDS) embedding of the invariant Gram matrix derived from global pairwise Tamura-Nei distances ($N=22$). The primary axis $Z_1$ (50.8\% variance) cleanly separates Subtype B references ($n=8$, blue circles) from Subtype C references ($n=8$, vermilion circles). Recombinant forms CRF07\_BC ($n=3$, green diamonds) and CRF08\_BC ($n=3$, purple squares) sit compressed at intermediate coordinates ($Z_1 \approx -0.03$ to $-0.04$). Whole-genome distances collapse mosaic structures into static averages, obscuring reticulate ancestry. \textbf  {(B)} Clonal Stationarity and Coalescent Wobble: Instantaneous Gower out-of-sample projected trajectory $Z_1(u)$ ($W=300\text  { nt}$, stride $10\text  { nt}$) along the 3,120-nucleotide \textit  {pol} gene for the 16 non-recombinant references. Both clades remain strictly stationary within their empirical envelopes (Subtype B mean $= +0.052$, flutter $\sigma = 0.008$; Subtype C mean $= -0.053$, flutter $\sigma = 0.012$). Point mutations generate local coalescent flutter, but unreticulated trajectories never cross the inter-clade divide ($Z_1 = 0$). \textbf  {(C)} Dynamic Recombinant Trajectories and Resolved Breakpoints: Continuous $Z_1(u)$ trajectories for CRF07\_BC (prototype AF286230, green) and CRF08\_BC (prototype AY008715, purple) plotted against shaded parental reference corridors. Aligned beneath is the HIV-1 \textit  {pol} functional domain track ($p6^*$, PR, RT, RNase H, IN). In Protease (PR), CRF07 tracks within Subtype B while CRF08 tracks within Subtype C. In Reverse Transcriptase, both lineages enter a Subtype B cassette. CRF08 crosses the zero-axis at nucleotide 894, entering approximately 60 nucleotides upstream of CRF07 (nucleotide 953). Both exit back into Subtype C at nucleotide $\sim 1,230$ and remain in Subtype C through Integrase. \textbf  {(D)} Metric Phase Space Dynamics: Continuous two-dimensional dynamical orbits in $(Z_1 \times Z_2)$ space. Non-recombinant parental lineages form stationary point basins at $(+0.05, 0.00)$ and $(-0.05, 0.04)$. Recombinant lineages trace smooth, open orbital loops that sweep across the inter-clade divide from $5'$ start positions (circles) to $3'$ terminal positions (squares) with tangent flow arrows. Continuous manifold geometry resolves distinct mosaic architectures in $O(N)$ time without combinatorial explosion.\relax }}{5}{figure.caption.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:theory_metric_trajectories}{{2}{5}{\textbf {Continuous sequence metric manifolds resolve competing retroviral chimeras in linear time without triplet enumeration.} \textbf {(A)} Canonical Sequence Metric Space: Classical multidimensional scaling (MDS) embedding of the invariant Gram matrix derived from global pairwise Tamura-Nei distances ($N=22$). The primary axis $Z_1$ (50.8\% variance) cleanly separates Subtype B references ($n=8$, blue circles) from Subtype C references ($n=8$, vermilion circles). Recombinant forms CRF07\_BC ($n=3$, green diamonds) and CRF08\_BC ($n=3$, purple squares) sit compressed at intermediate coordinates ($Z_1 \approx -0.03$ to $-0.04$). Whole-genome distances collapse mosaic structures into static averages, obscuring reticulate ancestry. \textbf {(B)} Clonal Stationarity and Coalescent Wobble: Instantaneous Gower out-of-sample projected trajectory $Z_1(u)$ ($W=300\text { nt}$, stride $10\text { nt}$) along the 3,120-nucleotide \textit {pol} gene for the 16 non-recombinant references. Both clades remain strictly stationary within their empirical envelopes (Subtype B mean $= +0.052$, flutter $\sigma = 0.008$; Subtype C mean $= -0.053$, flutter $\sigma = 0.012$). Point mutations generate local coalescent flutter, but unreticulated trajectories never cross the inter-clade divide ($Z_1 = 0$). \textbf {(C)} Dynamic Recombinant Trajectories and Resolved Breakpoints: Continuous $Z_1(u)$ trajectories for CRF07\_BC (prototype AF286230, green) and CRF08\_BC (prototype AY008715, purple) plotted against shaded parental reference corridors. Aligned beneath is the HIV-1 \textit {pol} functional domain track ($p6^*$, PR, RT, RNase H, IN). In Protease (PR), CRF07 tracks within Subtype B while CRF08 tracks within Subtype C. In Reverse Transcriptase, both lineages enter a Subtype B cassette. CRF08 crosses the zero-axis at nucleotide 894, entering approximately 60 nucleotides upstream of CRF07 (nucleotide 953). Both exit back into Subtype C at nucleotide $\sim 1,230$ and remain in Subtype C through Integrase. \textbf {(D)} Metric Phase Space Dynamics: Continuous two-dimensional dynamical orbits in $(Z_1 \times Z_2)$ space. Non-recombinant parental lineages form stationary point basins at $(+0.05, 0.00)$ and $(-0.05, 0.04)$. Recombinant lineages trace smooth, open orbital loops that sweep across the inter-clade divide from $5'$ start positions (circles) to $3'$ terminal positions (squares) with tangent flow arrows. Continuous manifold geometry resolves distinct mosaic architectures in $O(N)$ time without combinatorial explosion.\relax }{figure.caption.3}{}}
