\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Site-level directed attention, ancestral root sink decoupling, and cumulative Brownian bridge dynamics along recombinant genomes.} \textbf  {(A)} Site-Level Alignment and Position-Specific Attention Breakdown: Microscopic view across a 35-nucleotide window ($u = 532\text  {--}567\text  { nt}$) in HIV-1 \textit  {pol}. Query sequence CRF07\_BC is aligned against candidate donor Subtype B, parental home Subtype C, and the ancestral root consensus. The stacked bar chart displays instantaneous directed attention $[A_u(\text  {Root}), A_u(\text  {Donor}), A_u(\text  {Home})]$ summing strictly to $1.0$ at each nucleotide. Shared invariant sites allocate baseline attention to home Subtype C. Donor synapomorphies (sites 545--546) elevate Subtype B attention ($A_B = 0.51\text  {--}0.58$). Private autapomorphies (site 560) route into the ancestral Root Sink ($A_{\mathrm  {Root}} = 0.52$). Routing private autapomorphies to node zero prevents spurious leakage into candidate donor affinity. \textbf  {(B)} Ancestral Root Sink Decouples Private Mutational Noise from Reticulation. Under an episodic private mutational burst (Darren heterotachy trap, benchmark scenario 15000, $4.9\times $ rate acceleration across nucleotides $1,020\text  {--}1,412$), private autapomorphies ($n = 36$) spike Root Sink attention $A_u(\mathrm  {Root})$ (grey impulse bars and smoothed curve). Relative donor affinity (blue curve) remains flat at neutral baseline ($0.50$, dotted line). Under authentic genetic recombination (HIV-1 CRF07\_BC RT cassette, nucleotides $982\text  {--}1,187$), donor affinity surges coherently across the 205-nucleotide tract driven by donor synapomorphies ($n = 24$). Root Sink attention remains quiescent ($\approx 0.038$). \textbf  {(C)} Directed Taxa Attention and Discriminatory Site Raster: Instantaneous relative donor affinity $A_B(u) / (A_B(u) + A_C(u))$ for CRF07\_BC along the full 3,120-nucleotide \textit  {pol} gene, plotted above the discriminatory site raster (Subtype B synapomorphies, blue ticks; Subtype C synapomorphies, vermilion ticks; private autapomorphies, black ticks) and aligned protein domain track. Neutral expectation sits at $0.50$ (dotted line). In the introgressed Subtype B cassette (nucleotides 982--1,187, light blue shading), donor synapomorphies drive a sustained surge in relative affinity. \textbf  {(D)} Cumulative Attention Dynamics and Differential Bridge Inflections: Continuous differential attention flux $Y(u) = C_{\mathrm  {Donor}}(u) - C_{\mathrm  {Home}}(u)$ for CRF07\_BC (green curve, breakpoints at $982$ and $1,187\text  { nt}$) and CRF08\_BC (purple curve, breakpoints at $862$ and $1,169\text  { nt}$). In Protease, shared B-like mutations impart positive drift; across the RT cassette, donor affinity surges, producing a steep positive inflection; upon exiting into Integrase, negative drift resumes as home Subtype C affinity steadily dominates.\relax }}{7}{figure.caption.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:theory_attention_rope}{{3}{7}{\textbf {Site-level directed attention, ancestral root sink decoupling, and cumulative Brownian bridge dynamics along recombinant genomes.} \textbf {(A)} Site-Level Alignment and Position-Specific Attention Breakdown: Microscopic view across a 35-nucleotide window ($u = 532\text {--}567\text { nt}$) in HIV-1 \textit {pol}. Query sequence CRF07\_BC is aligned against candidate donor Subtype B, parental home Subtype C, and the ancestral root consensus. The stacked bar chart displays instantaneous directed attention $[A_u(\text {Root}), A_u(\text {Donor}), A_u(\text {Home})]$ summing strictly to $1.0$ at each nucleotide. Shared invariant sites allocate baseline attention to home Subtype C. Donor synapomorphies (sites 545--546) elevate Subtype B attention ($A_B = 0.51\text {--}0.58$). Private autapomorphies (site 560) route into the ancestral Root Sink ($A_{\mathrm {Root}} = 0.52$). Routing private autapomorphies to node zero prevents spurious leakage into candidate donor affinity. \textbf {(B)} Ancestral Root Sink Decouples Private Mutational Noise from Reticulation. Under an episodic private mutational burst (Darren heterotachy trap, benchmark scenario 15000, $4.9\times $ rate acceleration across nucleotides $1,020\text {--}1,412$), private autapomorphies ($n = 36$) spike Root Sink attention $A_u(\mathrm {Root})$ (grey impulse bars and smoothed curve). Relative donor affinity (blue curve) remains flat at neutral baseline ($0.50$, dotted line). Under authentic genetic recombination (HIV-1 CRF07\_BC RT cassette, nucleotides $982\text {--}1,187$), donor affinity surges coherently across the 205-nucleotide tract driven by donor synapomorphies ($n = 24$). Root Sink attention remains quiescent ($\approx 0.038$). \textbf {(C)} Directed Taxa Attention and Discriminatory Site Raster: Instantaneous relative donor affinity $A_B(u) / (A_B(u) + A_C(u))$ for CRF07\_BC along the full 3,120-nucleotide \textit {pol} gene, plotted above the discriminatory site raster (Subtype B synapomorphies, blue ticks; Subtype C synapomorphies, vermilion ticks; private autapomorphies, black ticks) and aligned protein domain track. Neutral expectation sits at $0.50$ (dotted line). In the introgressed Subtype B cassette (nucleotides 982--1,187, light blue shading), donor synapomorphies drive a sustained surge in relative affinity. \textbf {(D)} Cumulative Attention Dynamics and Differential Bridge Inflections: Continuous differential attention flux $Y(u) = C_{\mathrm {Donor}}(u) - C_{\mathrm {Home}}(u)$ for CRF07\_BC (green curve, breakpoints at $982$ and $1,187\text { nt}$) and CRF08\_BC (purple curve, breakpoints at $862$ and $1,169\text { nt}$). In Protease, shared B-like mutations impart positive drift; across the RT cassette, donor affinity surges, producing a steep positive inflection; upon exiting into Integrase, negative drift resumes as home Subtype C affinity steadily dominates.\relax }{figure.caption.4}{}}
